---
// UploadRight Architecture & Privacy Trust Component
// Grounded in technical reality without fake badges
---

<section class="py-16 sm:py-20 bg-white border-t border-[#D9D9DE]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 bg-[#F0F6FE] border border-[#0062FF]/20 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold text-[#0062FF] uppercase tracking-wider">
        Engine Architecture
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#101013] tracking-tight">
        Zero-Latency, Client-Side Image Engineering
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#626274] leading-relaxed">
        Why UploadRight is faster and inherently safer than legacy cloud converters: your sensitive identity documents never leave your browser sandbox.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 Core Architecture Pillars -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 sm:gap-8">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F7F8] border border-[#D9D9DE] space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#D9D9DE] flex items-center justify-center text-[#0062FF] shadow-xs">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2" />
            <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#101013]">100% In-Browser Privacy</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#626274] leading-relaxed">
          Traditional image websites upload your photo to external cloud servers, creating security risks. UploadRight processes every byte entirely inside your browser's local RAM using HTML5 Canvas. Zero network requests, zero database logs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F7F8] border border-[#D9D9DE] space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#D9D9DE] flex items-center justify-center text-[#0062FF] shadow-xs">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#101013]">Binary Search Size Targeting</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#626274] leading-relaxed">
          Government portals reject files that are even 1 byte above maximum or below minimum. Our deterministic binary-search compression iteratively hones in on the target byte boundary within 250 milliseconds while preserving visual sharpness.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F7F8] border border-[#D9D9DE] space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#D9D9DE] flex items-center justify-center text-[#0062FF] shadow-xs">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z" />
            <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8" />
            <line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13" />
            <line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17" />
            <polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#101013]">JFIF APP0 DPI Injection</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#626274] leading-relaxed">
          Portals like SSC, IBPS, and UPSC run automated header parsers looking for 200 or 300 DPI tags. UploadRight parses binary JPEG markers and safely injects big-endian resolution headers directly into APP0 segment metadata.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
